    {
      "type": "done",
      "answer": "Based on the lecture material, hazards are defined as any condition that causes the pipeline to stall, resulting in \"bubbles\" and degraded efficiency [S1]. The three types of hazards differ based on the specific cause of the stall:\n\n1.  **Data Hazards**: These occur due to dependencies on data. The lecture specifies three sub-types of data hazards:\n    *   Read-after-write (RAW)\n    *   Write-after-write (WAW)\n    *   Write-after-read (WAR) [S1].\n\n2.  **Control Hazards**: These occur due to branches and synchronization [S1]. The lecture notes that deeper pipelines can cause worse penalties for control hazards [S2].\n\n3.  **Structural Hazards**: These occur due to contention on hardware resources. Examples of such hardware include memory channels, cache slots, and queues [S1].\n\nIn summary, data hazards stem from data dependencies, control hazards stem from branching/synchronization logic, and structural hazards stem from physical hardware resource contention [S1].\n\n**Source:**\n*   Page 18 [S1]\n*   Page 20 [S2]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "document_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402",
          "chunk_id": "34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402-p18-1",
          "page": 18,
          "text": "CPU: Optimize Latency of a Small Number of Complex Threads\n Why Pipeline Stalls: Hazards\n\n¡ Any condition that causes the pipeline to\n   stall is called a hazard.\n\n   ¡  Result: Much bubbles and degraded efficiency\n¡ Various types of hazards\n\n   ¡  Data Hazard: Stall due to dependencies of some\n       data\n\n      ¡  Read-after-write (RAW)\n\n      ¡  Write-after-write (WAW)\n\n      ¡  Write-after-read (WAR)\n\n   ¡  Control Hazard: Stall due to branch and\n       synchronization\n\n   ¡  Structural hazard: Stall due to contention on\n      hardware such as memory channel, cache slot,\n      queue, etc.",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/34911c46e78edc833f283f8dd678b85d6f8c92d66859e6bf6886949181d95402/pages/18/preview",
          "source": "S1"
        },
